{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794595045020,"sessionID":"ses_e29cd1063ffeCxGmp1qmJeHmTZ","part":{"partID":"prt_1d6333712002MV3MkHr0cvFcVB","sessionID":"ses_e29cd1063ffeCxGmp1qmJeHmTZ","messageID":"msg_1d6331a69001Y3DU1fh4fpkyMl","type":"tool","id":"call_ab4c65be6f6b413f818de05b","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/hook-confirm-3b/invocation-metadata.json"},"output":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/hook-confirm-3b/invocation-metadata.json, lines 1-1\n1: {\"effectiveConfig\":{\"kind\":\"cli-opencode\",\"executable\":\"opencode\",\"executableVersion\":\"sha256:b9d576000191d7f441198076f6d50a843064259709ed31f7de995cbfc540d85f\",\"model\":\"opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash\",\"reasoningEffort\":\"max\",\"serviceTier\":null,\"sandboxMode\":\"danger-full-access\",\"permissionMode\":\"acceptEdits\",\"webSearch\":\"inherit\"},\"invocationFingerprint\":\"inv:60fcb4962bc2eb25cf725272cacdfccf8c6c17d2a3909ebba1330e840c635733\"}","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/hook-confirm-3b/invocation-metadata.json, lines 1-1\n1: {\"effectiveConfig\":{\"kind\":\"cli-opencode\",\"executable\":\"opencode\",\"executableVersion\":\"sha256:b9d576000191d7f441198076f6d50a843064259709ed31f7de995cbfc540d85f\",\"model\":\"opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash\",\"reasoningEffort\":\"max\",\"serviceTier\":null,\"sandboxMode\":\"danger-full-access\",\"permissionMode\":\"acceptEdits\",\"webSearch\":\"inherit\"},\"invocationFingerprint\":\"inv:60fcb4962bc2eb25cf725272cacdfccf8c6c17d2a3909ebba1330e840c635733\"}"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/hook-confirm-3b/invocation-metadata.json\"}"},"time":{"start":1794595043090,"end":1794595045020}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794595045025,"sessionID":"ses_e29cd1063ffeCxGmp1qmJeHmTZ","part":{"partID":"prt_1d633388f001xyFz30B6dR2uOj","sessionID":"ses_e29cd1063ffeCxGmp1qmJeHmTZ","messageID":"msg_1d6331a69001Y3DU1fh4fpkyMl","type":"tool","id":"call_7d8a21f2fa184a5a98a5026d","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Skilled/c9fe91ef-9b85-4bdc-88fb-4d6f766eaecf/scratchpad/review-instructions-3b.txt"},"output":"Read file /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Skilled/c9fe91ef-9b85-4bdc-88fb-4d6f766eaecf/scratchpad/review-instructions-3b.txt, lines 1-2\n1: Code review of command surfacing, PASS THREE confirming round. Commit 860610d783 fixed the two findings of pass three. Read `git -c core.fsmonitor=false show 860610d783 -- .skilled` and the whole of the two changed source files: .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs (the functions readWords, simpleCommands, commandWords, nodeFlagSkipsScript, runsNodeOnMarker, scriptWord, runsMarker) and the NO_EDIT_REQUEST pattern with isNoEditRequest in .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts, plus the callers of isNoEditRequest in runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts and runtime/lib/scorer/text.ts. Finding DR3-P1-001: a node flag that carries its value in the same word (`node -e1 <script>`, `node --eval=1 <script>`) was read as a launch of the hook script. Finding AR3-P2-001: `make no changes to its public api` inside a change request was read as a request for no change. Your work: (1) say whether each fix holds, by running a concrete input through the code (for the hook check, write a settings file under a mktemp folder and run `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs --root <folder>`, then remove the folder). (2) Look for a defect the fix introduced: a working hook command now reported as hook-missing, a non-launch still reported as ok, a real no-edit prompt that now keeps its command. (3) Report each as P0, P1 or P2 with file:line and the concrete input and output. A finding without a concrete input you ran is not a finding. Severity guide: P1 only when a hook command a person would plausibly write is misread, or a prompt a person would plausibly type is misrouted. An exotic shell construct is P2. Never open holdout-prompts.jsonl or read holdout prompt text. Change no code, write only inside your lineage folder. Single test files only: `node --test .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs` and `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD npx vitest run tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` from .skilled/skills/system... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n2: Your lineage label is the last folder of config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir. The hook-confirm-3b lineage reviews the hook check fix first and deepest, the noedit-confirm-3b lineage the no-edit pattern fix. Each still checks the other fix once.","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Skilled/c9fe91ef-9b85-4bdc-88fb-4d6f766eaecf/scratchpad/review-instructions-3b.txt, lines 1-2\n1: Code review of command surfacing, PASS THREE confirming round. Commit 860610d783 fixed the two findings of pass three. Read `git -c core.fsmonitor=false show 860610d783 -- .skilled` and the whole of the two changed source files: .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs (the functions readWords, simpleCommands, commandWords, nodeFlagSkipsScript, runsNodeOnMarker, scriptWord, runsMarker) and the NO_EDIT_REQUEST pattern with isNoEditRequest in .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts, plus the callers of isNoEditRequest in runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts and runtime/lib/scorer/text.ts. Finding DR3-P1-001: a node flag that carries its value in the same word (`node -e1 <script>`, `node --eval=1 <script>`) was read as a launch of the hook script. Finding AR3-P2-001: `make no changes to its public api` inside a change request was read as a request for no change. Your work: (1) say whether each fix holds, by running a concrete input through the code (for the hook check, write a settings file under a mktemp folder and run `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs --root <folder>`, then remove the folder). (2) Look for a defect the fix introduced: a working hook command now reported as hook-missing, a non-launch still reported as ok, a real no-edit prompt that now keeps its command. (3) Report each as P0, P1 or P2 with file:line and the concrete input and output. A finding without a concrete input you ran is not a finding. Severity guide: P1 only when a hook command a person would plausibly write is misread, or a prompt a person would plausibly type is misrouted. An exotic shell construct is P2. Never open holdout-prompts.jsonl or read holdout prompt text. Change no code, write only inside your lineage folder. Single test files only: `node --test .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs` and `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD npx vitest run tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` from .skilled/skills/system... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n2: Your lineage label is the last folder of config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir. The hook-confirm-3b lineage reviews the hook check fix first and deepest, the noedit-confirm-3b lineage the no-edit pattern fix. Each still checks the other fix once."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Skilled/c9fe91ef-9b85-4bdc-88fb-4d6f766eaecf/scratchpad/review-instructions-3b.txt\"}"},"time":{"start":1794595043471,"end":1794595045025}}}}
