{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794595052636,"sessionID":"ses_e29cd1063ffeCxGmp1qmJeHmTZ","part":{"partID":"prt_1d6335556002FuMbAauD2sVG8Z","sessionID":"ses_e29cd1063ffeCxGmp1qmJeHmTZ","messageID":"msg_1d633424b00133HcN40As2SZ1L","type":"tool","id":"call_6d0def87a81c45798499faf8","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && wc -c /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Skilled/c9fe91ef-9b85-4bdc-88fb-4d6f766eaecf/scratchpad/review-instructions-3b.txt && cat /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Skilled/c9fe91ef-9b85-4bdc-88fb-4d6f766eaecf/scratchpad/review-instructions-3b.txt"},"output":"    2318 /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Skilled/c9fe91ef-9b85-4bdc-88fb-4d6f766eaecf/scratchpad/review-instructions-3b.txt\nCode review of command surfacing, PASS THREE confirming round. Commit 860610d783 fixed the two findings of pass three. Read `git -c core.fsmonitor=false show 860610d783 -- .skilled` and the whole of the two changed source files: .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs (the functions readWords, simpleCommands, commandWords, nodeFlagSkipsScript, runsNodeOnMarker, scriptWord, runsMarker) and the NO_EDIT_REQUEST pattern with isNoEditRequest in .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts, plus the callers of isNoEditRequest in runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts and runtime/lib/scorer/text.ts. Finding DR3-P1-001: a node flag that carries its value in the same word (`node -e1 <script>`, `node --eval=1 <script>`) was read as a launch of the hook script. Finding AR3-P2-001: `make no changes to its public api` inside a change request was read as a request for no change. Your work: (1) say whether each fix holds, by running a concrete input through the code (for the hook check, write a settings file under a mktemp folder and run `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs --root <folder>`, then remove the folder). (2) Look for a defect the fix introduced: a working hook command now reported as hook-missing, a non-launch still reported as ok, a real no-edit prompt that now keeps its command. (3) Report each as P0, P1 or P2 with file:line and the concrete input and output. A finding without a concrete input you ran is not a finding. Severity guide: P1 only when a hook command a person would plausibly write is misread, or a prompt a person would plausibly type is misrouted. An exotic shell construct is P2. Never open holdout-prompts.jsonl or read holdout prompt text. Change no code, write only inside your lineage folder. Single test files only: `node --test .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs` and `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD npx vitest run tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` from .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime. No build, no full suite, no daemon, no model CLI.\nYour lineage label is the last folder of config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir. The hook-confirm-3b lineage reviews the hook check fix first and deepest, the noedit-confirm-3b lineage the no-edit pattern fix. Each still checks the other fix once.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"    2318 /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Skilled/c9fe91ef-9b85-4bdc-88fb-4d6f766eaecf/scratchpad/review-instructions-3b.txt\nCode review of command surfacing, PASS THREE confirming round. Commit 860610d783 fixed the two findings of pass three. Read `git -c core.fsmonitor=false show 860610d783 -- .skilled` and the whole of the two changed source files: .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs (the functions readWords, simpleCommands, commandWords, nodeFlagSkipsScript, runsNodeOnMarker, scriptWord, runsMarker) and the NO_EDIT_REQUEST pattern with isNoEditRequest in .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts, plus the callers of isNoEditRequest in runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts and runtime/lib/scorer/text.ts. Finding DR3-P1-001: a node flag that carries its value in the same word (`node -e1 <script>`, `node --eval=1 <script>`) was read as a launch of the hook script. Finding AR3-P2-001: `make no changes to its public api` inside a change request was read as a request for no change. Your work: (1) say whether each fix holds, by running a concrete input through the code (for the hook check, write a settings file under a mktemp folder and run `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs --root <folder>`, then remove the folder). (2) Look for a defect the fix introduced: a working hook command now reported as hook-missing, a non-launch still reported as ok, a real no-edit prompt that now keeps its command. (3) Report each as P0, P1 or P2 with file:line and the concrete input and output. A finding without a concrete input you ran is not a finding. Severity guide: P1 only when a hook command a person would plausibly write is misread, or a prompt a person would plausibly type is misrouted. An exotic shell construct is P2. Never open holdout-prompts.jsonl or read holdout prompt text. Change no code, write only inside your lineage folder. Single test files only: `node --test .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs` and `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD npx vitest run tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` from .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime. No build, no full suite, no daemon, no model CLI.\nYour lineage label is the last folder of config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir. The hook-confirm-3b lineage reviews the hook check fix first and deepest, the noedit-confirm-3b lineage the no-edit pattern fix. Each still checks the other fix once.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-r