{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794595614887,"sessionID":"ses_e29cd1063ffeCxGmp1qmJeHmTZ","part":{"partID":"prt_1d63bd694001Dg00Mm0NSlFbDG","sessionID":"ses_e29cd1063ffeCxGmp1qmJeHmTZ","messageID":"msg_1d63bbf34001DxQqW5rOnry6F1","type":"tool","id":"call_ed338b583f734b57b090731f","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/hook-confirm-3b/deep-review-strategy.md","oldString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n\n## 8A. WHAT FAILED\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]","newString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n- Driving the real CLI against a settings root per command: `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs --root <probe>` distinguishes the fix from a regression in one run, and the paired `printf '' | node - <script>` probe proves what node actually executes rather than what the reader assumes (iteration 1).\n- Reading the flag grammar from node's own behaviour (`node -rc /dev/null` -> `bad option`) instead of inferring it from the flag tables (iteration 1).\n\n## 8A. WHAT FAILED\n- Relying on the commit's suite claim as evidence: the dispatch permits only the two named single test files, so the claim was treated as unverified prose and the CLI probes carried the proof instead (iteration 1)."},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/hook-confirm-3b/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/hook-confirm-3b/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/hook-confirm-3b/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/hook-confirm-3b/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/hook-confirm-3b/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -55,12 +55,13 @@\n | advisor-runtime | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` |\n | advisor-runtime | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` |\n \n ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n-[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n+- Driving the real CLI against a settings root per command: `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs --root <probe>` distinguishes the fix from a regression in one run, and the paired `printf '' | node - <script>` probe proves what node actually executes rather than what the reader assumes (iteration 1).\n+- Reading the flag grammar from node's own behaviour (`node -rc /dev/null` -> `bad option`) instead of inferring it from the flag tables (iteration 1).\n \n ## 8A. WHAT FAILED\n-[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n+- Relying on the commit's suite claim as evidence: the dispatch permits only the two named single test files, so the claim was treated as unverified prose and the CLI probes carried the proof instead (iteration 1).\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n ## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n [No exhausted approach categories yet]\n","status":"modified","additions":3,"deletions":2}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/hook-confirm-3b/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/hook-confirm-3b/deep-review-strategy.md\",\"oldString\":\"## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n\\n## 8A. WHAT FAILED\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\",\"newString\":\"## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n- Driving the real CLI against a settings root per command: `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs --root <probe>` distinguishes the fix from a regression in one run, and the paired `printf '' | node - <script>` probe proves what node actually executes rather than what the reader assumes (iteration 1).\\n- Reading the flag grammar from node's own behaviour (`node -rc /dev/null` -> `bad option`) instead of inferring it from the flag tables (iteration 1).\\n\\n## 8A. WHAT FAILED\\n- Relying on the commit's suite claim as evidence: the dispatch permits only the two named single test files, so the claim was treated as unverified prose and the CLI probes carried the proof instead (iteration 1).\"}"},"time":{"start":1794595608212,"end":1794595614887}}}}
