{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794595767577,"sessionID":"ses_e29cd1063ffeCxGmp1qmJeHmTZ","part":{"partID":"prt_1d63dd4ab001tStG9draiX35Po","sessionID":"ses_e29cd1063ffeCxGmp1qmJeHmTZ","messageID":"msg_1d63dc2d7001bk25aYNB4ByYPL","type":"tool","id":"call_f47b1e11be9a4055b3fa6fc6","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 002 - hook-confirm-3b\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Lineage: `hook-confirm-3b`, session `fanout-hook-confirm-3b-1794595021404-69frey`, iteration 2 of 3.\n- Review focus (binding): the no-edit half of commit `860610d783` is checked once here; every finding needs file:line and a concrete input run.\n- How this iteration addressed the focus: it reads `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` and `isNoEditRequest` in full, reads all three callers, and runs the same prompts through the pre-commit module (`git show 860610d783^:...`) and the current module side by side, so the before/after delta is measured rather than asserted.\n\n## Dimension\n\nCorrectness.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:283-295` — `NO_EDIT_REQUEST`, `isNoEditRequest`.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:326-345` — `attachCommand` and its no-edit early return.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:675-690` — `readOnlyRouteAllowed`.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:877-886` — `commandMeaningEligible`.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/text.ts:147-160` — `isReadOnlyExplainer`.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:30-77` — `NOEDIT4` and the scope-limit table.\n- Pre-commit module extracted with `git show 860610d783^:.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` into `probes/command-attach-pre.ts` for the before/after comparison.\n\n## Findings by Severity\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\n1. **The `make no changes` lookahead is over-broad: a genuine no-edit request that names its object loses the guard** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:289` -- the added `(?! (?:to|in)\\b)` makes the shared no-edit predicate return `false` for every sentence of the form `make no changes to <object>`, including sentences that rule out all changes and merely say what the object is. The guard then stops withholding a mutating command, so a reader who explicitly ruled out a change is handed `/create:agent`.\n   Finding class: correctness (regression introduced by `860610d783`; the fix's own test table covers only the direction it fixed).\n   Scope proof: line 289 is the changed line in a declared-scope file; `attachCommand` at `command-attach.ts:335` and both scorer callers consume the same predicate, so the regression reaches every no-edit gate.\n   Affected surface hints: `attachCommand` hub-command gate, `readOnlyRouteAllowed` (`fusion.ts:677`), `commandMeaningEligible` (`fusion.ts:881`), `isReadOnlyExplainer` (`text.ts:150`).\n   Case: the prompt `make no changes to any file, just report what you find` is a plain no-edit request. Before the commit the predicate matched `make no changes` and `attachCommand` returned `undefined`; after the commit the predicate returns `false` and `attachCommand` returns `'/create:agent'` for a single-mode mutating route.\n\n   Concrete inputs run (current module vs pre-commit module, node v26.13.0):\n\n   ```\n   prompt: \"make no changes to any file, just report what you find\"\n     post-fix isNoEditRequest = false   attachCommand = \"/create:agent\"\n     pre-fix  isNoEditRequest = true    attachCommand = undefined\n   prompt: \"make no changes to the code, just analyze the parser\"\n     post-fix isNoEditRequest = false   attachCommand = \"/create:agent\"\n     pre-fix  isNoEditRequest = true    attachCommand = undefined\n   ```\n\n   Why P1: a prompt a person would plausibly type is misrouted, which is exactly the operator guide's P1 bar. The old wording (`make no changes` alone) is covered by `NOEDIT4` at `tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:30-34`; the new exclusion removes the object-bearing form from the same class, and no replacement phrase (`just show`, `just list`, `do not change`) is required to be present. The suite still passes 26/26 because no test row exercises a genuine no-edit request that names its object.\n\n   Claim adjudication:\n\n   ```json\n   {\n     \"type\": \"correctness-regression\",\n     \"claim\": \"The added negative lookahead at command-attach.ts:289 disables the shared no-edit gate for genuine no-edit requests phrased as 'make no changes to <object>', so a mutating hub command is offered where it was withheld before the commit.\",\n     \"evidenceRefs\": [\"command-attach.ts:289\", \"command-attach.ts:335\", \"fusion.ts:677\", \"fusion.ts:881\", \"text.ts:150\", \"iterations/iteration-002.md probe output\"],\n     \"counterevidenceSought\": \"Checked every other alternative in NO_EDIT_REQUEST against the failing prompt ('no edits?', 'no changes yet', 'without making changes', 'do not change', 'read-only only', 'only; do not', 'just show', 'just list'); none matches, and no other caller re-checks a scope noun. Also ran the pre-commit module to confirm the guard fired before the change.\",\n     \"alternativeExplanation\": \"The change may be intended to treat every 'make no changes to X' as a scope limit. Rejected: the predicate's own contract is 'Wording that asks for an answer and rules out a change', and the existing NOEDIT4 table treats bare 'make no changes' as that wording. Only a change verb elsewhere in the prompt distinguishes the two readings, and the predicate cannot see one.\",\n     \"finalSeverity\": \"P1\",\n     \"confidence\": 0.9,\n     \"downgradeTrigger\": \"Downgrade to P2 if the no-edit gate's contract is amended to exclude every object-bearing 'make no changes' form, or if a caller is shown to re-add a change-verb check before offering a mutating command.\"\n   }\n   ```\n\n### P2 Findings\n\n1. **The lookahead's word list is too narrow: an adverb or a different preposition keeps the old false no-edit reading** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:289` -- the exclusion covers only a directly following `to` or `in`, so `make no changes whatsoever to ...` (and `make no changes on ...`) still matches inside a change request and withholds the command. That is the `AR3-P2-001` failure mode the commit set out to close, still reachable.\n   Finding class: correctness (incomplete fix).\n   Scope proof: same changed line; the input is a change request of the same shape as the two rows the commit added.\n   Affected surface hints: `attachCommand` hub-command gate; scorer no-edit gates.\n   Case: `refactor the parser and make no changes whatsoever to its public api` is a change request with a scope limit; it is read as a no-edit request and loses its command.\n\n   Concrete inputs run:\n\n   ```\n   prompt: \"make no changes whatsoever to the public api\"\n     post-fix isNoEditRequest = true   attachCommand = undefined\n     pre-fix  isNoEditRequest = true   attachCommand = undefined   (unchanged)\n   prompt: \"make no changes to its public api\"       -> false  (fix target holds)\n   prompt: \"make no changes in the tests\"            -> false  (fix target holds)\n   ```\n\n   Why P2 and not P1: the wording needs an intervening adverb to fail, and the consequence is a withheld command rather than a mutation offered against an explicit instruction. The operator guide rates the plausible-but-narrower misroute as advisory, and the pass-three finding it mirrors (`AR3-P2-001`) was itself P2.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n- `spec_code` — **partial**. The commit message says: \"The no-edit pattern read a change request that says what to leave alone ... as a request for no change at all. That wording now keeps its command.\" The named wording does keep its command (`make no changes to its public api` -> `false`, `make no changes in the tests` -> `false`), so the stated mechanism is present at `command-attach.ts:289`. The same sentence also implies the pattern still reads *genuine* no-edit wording as no-edit; that half is now false for the object-bearing form, which is P1 finding 1.\n- `checklist_evidence` — **notApplicable**: no `checklist.md` in the packet.\n- `skill_agent` — **pass**: `attachCommand`'s early return at `command-attach.ts:335` calls the shared predicate, so the hub-command gate inherits the same behaviour; no drift between the two gates.\n- `agent_cross_runtime` — notApplicable (no runtime mirror in this diff).\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- Exact surfaces checked: `attachCommand` (`command-attach.ts:326-345`), `readOnlyRouteAllowed` (`fusion.ts:675-690`), `commandMeaningEligible` (`fusion.ts:877-886`), `isReadOnlyExplainer` (`text.ts:147-160`). All four consume `isNoEditRequest`, and no caller adds its own object/verb check.\n- Exact surface exercised: `attachCommand('sk-doc', {action:'route',selectionKind:'single',targets:[{workflowMode:'sk-create-agent'}]}, <prompt>)`, the same route shape the guard tests use, run against both the current and the pre-commit module.\n- Suite run permitted by the dispatch: `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD npx vitest run tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` from `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime` -> **26 passed, 0 failed**. A green suite with the P1 present is evidence that the table lacks a genuine-no-edit-with-object row, not evidence that the predicate is right.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\nThe fix target itself holds (each prompt run through the current module):\n\n| Prompt | `isNoEditRequest` |\n|---|---|\n| `make no changes to its public api` | false |\n| `make no changes in the tests` | false |\n| `refactor the parser and make no changes to its public api` | false |\n| `rename the helper but make no changes in the tests` | false |\n\nThe unchanged no-edit forms still fire: `make no changes` -> true, `make no changes, just analyze` -> true, `do not change anything` -> true, `just show me the plan` -> true, curly-apostrophe `don’t touch any files` -> true.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- The pre-commit module was extracted into `probes/command-attach-pre.ts` rather than checked out, so the review target stayed read-only and the comparison module stayed inside the lineage. Both modules have no imports, so the two runs differ only in the pattern line.\n- A prompt that combines a scope limit with another old no-edit phrase still reads as no-edit and still withholds the command: the P1 bites only when no other alternative matches. Recorded so the severity is not read as \"every change request is now offered a command\".\n- A prompt that names the artifact surface as a genuine no-edit request and also names a change verb elsewhere in the sentence is genuinely ambiguous; the predicate cannot separate the readings, which is the root cause behind both findings.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- \"The fix breaks the original `AR3-P2-001` case\": ruled out — both commit-added rows and the predicate return `false`.\n- \"Another alternative in `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` catches the failing prompt\": ruled out by enumerating all nine alternatives against `make no changes to any file, just report what you find`; none matches.\n- \"A caller compensates with a second check\": ruled out by reading all three call sites — none inspects the sentence beyond the predicate.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: maintainability (then traceability).\n- Focus area: test-table completeness for the no-edit predicate and the hook check, the commit's own claims, and whether the two P2s stay advisory at synthesis.\n- Reason: correctness coverage is now complete on both halves of the diff; the remaining question is whether the tests would have caught the P1 and whether any packet doc claims otherwise.\n- Rotation status: correctness rotates out.\n- Required evidence: the two named test files run green, and the exact test-table gaps cited by line.\n\n## Verdict\n\nThe no-edit fix holds for the case it targeted but introduced a P1 regression in the opposite direction and leaves the old class reachable through an adverb. Active P1 with no P0.\n\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/hook-confirm-3b/iterations/iteration-002.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/hook-confirm-3b/iterations/iteration-002.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/hook-confirm-3b/iterations/iteration-002.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Iteration 002 - hook-confirm-3b\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Lineage: `hook-confirm-3b`, session `fanout-hook-confirm-3b-1794595021404-69frey`, iteration 2 of 3.\\n- Review focus (binding): the no-edit half of commit `860610d783` is checked once here; every finding needs file:line and a concrete input run.\\n- How this iteration addressed the focus: it reads `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` and `isNoEditRequest` in full, reads all three callers, and runs the same prompts through the pre-commit module (`git show 860610d783^:...`) and the current module side by side, so the before/after delta is measured rather than asserted.\\n\\n## Dimension\\n\\nCorrectness.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:283-295` — `NO_EDIT_REQUEST`, `isNoEditRequest`.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:326-345` — `attachCommand` and its no-edit early return.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:675-690` — `readOnlyRouteAllowed`.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:877-886` — `commandMeaningEligible`.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/text.ts:147-160` — `isReadOnlyExplainer`.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:30-77` — `NOEDIT4` and the scope-limit table.\\n- Pre-commit module extracted with `git show 860610d783^:.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` into `probes/command-attach-pre.ts` for the before/after comparison.\\n\\n## Findings by Severity\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\n1. **The `make no changes` lookahead is over-broad: a genuine no-edit request that names its object loses the guard** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:289` -- the added `(?! (?:to|in)\\\\b)` makes the shared no-edit predicate return `false` for every sentence of the form `make no changes to <object>`, including sentences that rule out all changes and merely say what the object is. The guard then stops withholding a mutating command, so a reader who explicitly ruled out a change is handed `/create:agent`.\\n   Finding class: correctness (regression introduced by `860610d783`; the fix's own test table covers only the direction it fixed).\\n   Scope proof: line 289 is the changed line in a declared-scope file; `attachCommand` at `command-attach.ts:335` and both scorer callers consume the same predicate, so the regression reaches every no-edit gate.\\n   Affected surface hints: `attachCommand` hub-command gate, `readOnlyRouteAllowed` (`fusion.ts:677`), `commandMeaningEligible` (`fusion.ts:881`), `isReadOnlyExplainer` (`text.ts:150`).\\n   Case: the prompt `make no changes to any file, just report what you find` is a plain no-edit request. Before the commit the predicate matched `make no changes` and `attachCommand` returned `undefined`; after the commit the predicate returns `false` and `attachCommand` returns `'/create:agent'` for a single-mode mutating route.\\n\\n   Concrete inputs run (current module vs pre-commit module, node v26.13.0):\\n\\n   ```\\n   prompt: \\\"make no changes to any file, just report what you find\\\"\\n     post-fix isNoEditRequest = false   attachCommand = \\\"/create:agent\\\"\\n     pre-fix  isNoEditRequest = true    attachCommand = undefined\\n   prompt: \\\"make no changes to the code, just analyze the parser\\\"\\n     post-fix isNoEditRequest = false   attachCommand = \\\"/create:agent\\\"\\n     pre-fix  isNoEditRequest = true    attachCommand = undefined\\n   ```\\n\\n   Why P1: a prompt a person would plausibly type is misrouted, which is exactly the operator guide's P1 bar. The old wording (`make no changes` alone) is covered by `NOEDIT4` at `tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:30-34`; the new exclusion removes the object-bearing form from the same class, and no replacement phrase (`just show`, `just list`, `do not change`) is required to be present. The suite still passes 26/26 because no test row exercises a genuine no-edit request that names its object.\\n\\n   Claim adjudication:\\n\\n   ```json\\n   {\\n     \\\"type\\\": \\\"correctness-regression\\\",\\n     \\\"claim\\\": \\\"The added negative lookahead at command-attach.ts:289 disables the shared no-edit gate for genuine no-edit requests phrased as 'make no changes to <object>', so a mutating hub command is offered where it was withheld before the commit.\\\",\\n     \\\"evidenceRefs\\\": [\\\"command-attach.ts:289\\\", \\\"command-attach.ts:335\\\", \\\"fusion.ts:677\\\", \\\"fusion.ts:881\\\", \\\"text.ts:150\\\", \\\"iterations/iteration-002.md probe output\\\"],\\n     \\\"counterevidenceSought\\\": \\\"Checked every other alternative in NO_EDIT_REQUEST against the failing prompt ('no edits?', 'no changes yet', 'without making changes', 'do not change', 'read-only only', 'only; do not', 'just show', 'just list'); none matches, and no other caller re-checks a scope noun. Also ran the pre-commit module to confirm the guard fired before the change.\\\",\\n     \\\"alternativeExplanation\\\": \\\"The change may be intended to treat every 'make no changes to X' as a scope limit. Rejected: the predicate's own contract is 'Wording that asks for an answer and rules out a change', and the existing NOEDIT4 table treats bare 'make no changes' as that wording. Only a change verb elsewhere in the prompt distinguishes the two readings, and the predicate cannot see one.\\\",\\n     \\\"finalSeverity\\\": \\\"P1\\\",\\n     \\\"confidence\\\": 0.9,\\n     \\\"downgradeTrigger\\\": \\\"Downgrade to P2 if the no-edit gate's contract is amended to exclude every object-bearing 'make no changes' form, or if a caller is shown to re-add a change-verb check before offering a mutating command.\\\"\\n   }\\n   ```\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\n1. **The lookahead's word list is too narrow: an adverb or a different preposition keeps the old false no-edit reading** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:289` -- the exclusion covers only a directly following `to` or `in`, so `make no changes whatsoever to ...` (and `make no changes on ...`) still matches inside a change request and withholds the command. That is the `AR3-P2-001` failure mode the commit set out to close, still reachable.\\n   Finding class: correctness (incomplete fix).\\n   Scope proof: same changed line; the input is a change request of the same shape as the two rows the commit added.\\n   Affected surface hints: `attachCommand` hub-command gate; scorer no-edit gates.\\n   Case: `refactor the parser and make no changes whatsoever to its public api` is a change request with a scope limit; it is read as a no-edit request and loses its command.\\n\\n   Concrete inputs run:\\n\\n   ```\\n   prompt: \\\"make no changes whatsoever to the public api\\\"\\n     post-fix isNoEditRequest = true   attachCommand = undefined\\n     pre-fix  isNoEditRequest = true   attachCommand = undefined   (unchanged)\\n   prompt: \\\"make no changes to its public api\\\"       -> false  (fix target holds)\\n   prompt: \\\"make no changes in the tests\\\"            -> false  (fix target holds)\\n   ```\\n\\n   Why P2 and not P1: the wording needs an intervening adverb to fail, and the consequence is a withheld command rather than a mutation offered against an explicit instruction. The operator guide rates the plausible-but-narrower misroute as advisory, and the pass-three finding it mirrors (`AR3-P2-001`) was itself P2.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n- `spec_code` — **partial**. The commit message says: \\\"The no-edit pattern read a change request that says what to leave alone ... as a request for no change at all. That wording now keeps its command.\\\" The named wording does keep its command (`make no changes to its public api` -> `false`, `make no changes in the tests` -> `false`), so the stated mechanism is present at `command-attach.ts:289`. The same sentence also implies the pattern still reads *genuine* no-edit wording as no-edit; that half is now false for the object-bearing form, which is P1 finding 1.\\n- `checklist_evidence` — **notApplicable**: no `checklist.md` in the packet.\\n- `skill_agent` — **pass**: `attachCommand`'s early return at `command-attach.ts:335` calls the shared predicate, so the hub-command gate inherits the same behaviour; no drift between the two gates.\\n- `agent_cross_runtime` — notApplicable (no runtime mirror in this diff).\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- Exact surfaces checked: `attachCommand` (`command-attach.ts:326-345`), `readOnlyRouteAllowed` (`fusion.ts:675-690`), `commandMeaningEligible` (`fusion.ts:877-886`), `isReadOnlyExplainer` (`text.ts:147-160`). All four consume `isNoEditRequest`, and no caller adds its own object/verb check.\\n- Exact surface exercised: `attachCommand('sk-doc', {action:'route',selectionKind:'single',targets:[{workflowMode:'sk-create-agent'}]}, <prompt>)`, the same route shape the guard tests use, run against both the current and the pre-commit module.\\n- Suite run permitted by the dispatch: `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD npx vitest run tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` from `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime` -> **26 passed, 0 failed**. A green suite with the P1 present is evidence that the table lacks a genuine-no-edit-with-object row, not evidence that the predicate is right.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\nThe fix target itself holds (each prompt run through the current module):\\n\\n| Prompt | `isNoEditRequest` |\\n|---|---|\\n| `make no changes to its public api` | false |\\n| `make no changes in the tests` | false |\\n| `refactor the parser and make no changes to its public api` | false |\\n| `rename the helper but make no changes in the tests` | false |\\n\\nThe unchanged no-edit forms still fire: `make no changes` -> true, `make no changes, just analyze` -> true, `do not change anything` -> true, `just show me the plan` -> true, curly-apostrophe `don’t touch any files` -> true.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- The pre-commit module was extracted into `probes/command-attach-pre.ts` rather than checked out, so the review target stayed read-only and the comparison module stayed inside the lineage. Both modules have no imports, so the two runs differ only in the pattern line.\\n- A prompt that combines a scope limit with another old no-edit phrase still reads as no-edit and still withholds the command: the P1 bites only when no other alternative matches. Recorded so the severity is not read as \\\"every change request is now offered a command\\\".\\n- A prompt that names the artifact surface as a genuine no-edit request and also names a change verb elsewhere in the sentence is genuinely ambiguous; the predicate cannot separate the readings, which is the root cause behind both findings.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- \\\"The fix breaks the original `AR3-P2-001` case\\\": ruled out — both commit-added rows and the predicate return `false`.\\n- \\\"Another alternative in `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` catches the failing prompt\\\": ruled out by enumerating all nine alternatives against `make no changes to any file, just report what you find`; none matches.\\n- \\\"A caller compensates with a second check\\\": ruled out by reading all three call sites — none inspects the sentence beyond the predicate.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: maintainability (then traceability).\\n- Focus area: test-table completeness for the no-edit predicate and the hook check, the commit's own claims, and whether the two P2s stay advisory at synthesis.\\n- Reason: correctness coverage is now complete on both halves of the diff; the remaining question is whether the tests would have caught the P1 and whether any packet doc claims otherwise.\\n- Rotation status: correctness rotates out.\\n- Required evidence: the two named test files run green, and the exact test-table gaps cited by line.\\n\\n## Verdict\\n\\nThe no-edit fix holds for the case it targeted but introduced a P1 regression in the opposite direction and leaves the old class reachable through an adverb. Active P1 with no P0.\\n\\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/hook-confirm-3b/iterations/iteration-002.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794595738795,"end":1794595767577}}}}
