{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794595925186,"sessionID":"ses_e29cd1063ffeCxGmp1qmJeHmTZ","part":{"id":"prt_1d640acc2001X22DGFAEwQgj7J","sessionID":"ses_e29cd1063ffeCxGmp1qmJeHmTZ","messageID":"msg_1d6409c80001f6wesLSkw6CwFZ","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794595929704,"sessionID":"ses_e29cd1063ffeCxGmp1qmJeHmTZ","part":{"partID":"prt_1d640ba19002wlP43RKgzI1mDP","sessionID":"ses_e29cd1063ffeCxGmp1qmJeHmTZ","messageID":"msg_1d6409c80001f6wesLSkw6CwFZ","type":"tool","id":"call_debd485ed55c4997bc4483b2","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && rg -n \"REQ-001|no-edit wording|no-edit\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/spec.md | head -20 && echo \"---AC001---\" && sed -n '50,60p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/acceptance-criteria.md"},"output":"3:description: \"Review pass two confirmed 27 P2 findings and no P0 or P1. Four no-edit wordings still attach a writing command, a backfill runs code from any folder a run log names, a file name with a space survives the restore and the doctor checks misread common hook launches. This phase fixes all 27 in ten file-disjoint work groups, with a failing-then-passing test wherever one can fail, and moves no floor.\"\n48:- One no-edit test shared by the attach path, the scorer's two command gates and the read-only explainer, which catches the common straight and curly wordings and moves no floor.\n59:Four no-edit wordings, \"don't change anything yet\", \"no changes yet\", \"don't touch any files\" written with a curly apostrophe and \"make no changes\", still attach `/create:agent` on the hub path and still pass the scorer's command gate, because the shared pattern knows only \"do not\". A backfill runs whatever advisor CLI and prompt hook sit in a folder a run log names. A created file whose name holds a space survives the restore. A started-command row picked with `--row-id` runs under the default arm, and its backfill replays a different fixture than the run used. The command capture leaves six environment variables changed in its caller, the cost script measures the child brief inside a dispatched worker and a busy marker after 1 MiB of stderr gets no retry. The hook-wiring check reports `hook-missing` for `env node`, `bash -lc` and five more working launches, and A10 counts two report-only copies as expected. Nine docs, comments and contracts say something the code no longer does.\n93:# PL/probe-no-edit.mts, exit 0\n113:# PL/probe-no-edit-corpus.mjs, exit 0\n283:- A. Widen the shared no-edit pattern, normalise curly apostrophes before the test in one exported helper and route the attach path, the scorer's two gates and the explainer through it. Guard status privacy with a stored record, drop the vacuous assertion, name `mutating` in the README row shape and escape line breaks in `tsString` (WG1).\n328:| REQ-001 | `SA2-P2-002`: `command-attach.ts` exports `isNoEditRequest(text)`, which lowercases, maps U+2018 and U+2019 to a straight apostrophe and tests a `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` widened with `make no changes`, `no changes yet` and the `don't` contraction. The plan first named a bare `no changes`, which a verifier showed catching change requests that limit their scope, so T042 narrowed it. `attachCommand`, `readOnlyRouteAllowed`, `commandMeaningEligible` and `isReadOnlyExplainer` call it, so the four wordings attach no command, fail both gates and read as no-write on a read-only prompt. |\n373:- **SC-001**: The planning probes print the fixed behaviour: `probe-no-edit.mts` prints `undefined` on all five attach lines and `false` on all five scorer lines, `probe-backfill-trust.mjs` prints `fake CLI ran: false, fake hook ran: false`, `probe-restore-quoted.mjs` prints `left on disk: notes draft.md false, plain.md false`, `probe-arm-fixture.mjs` prints `--row-id g2-deep-review-ask -> arm g2` and `refused mixed_row_arms`, `probe-capture-env.mjs` prints `variables left changed: []`, `probe-cost-child.mjs` prints `hook saw AI_SESSION_CHILD=<unset>`, `probe-busy-cap.mts` prints `marker after 1 MiB: errorCode SQLITE_BUSY_EXHAUSTED, retriesAttempted 1`, `probe-hook-shapes.cjs` prints `exit 0 ok claude` for the nine launch shapes and `hook-missing` for both `echo` shapes, and `probe-a10-count.sh` prints `3/6 copies as expected, 2 reported only, 1 pointer missing`.\n421:- \"do not change anything yet\" still matches, and a prompt with no no-edit wording still attaches `/create:agent`.\n434:| Risk | 9/25 | The no-edit gate and the backfill trust are offer-safety and code-execution guards, each behind a failing-then-passing test and the floors |\n---AC001---\n## 2. CRITERIA\n\nOne row per criterion. `AC-ID` is stable once written: supersede a criterion, never renumber it. A new row takes the highest AC-ID plus one. The short names are the ones `tasks.md` defines in its Task Notation. Every reading ran on base commit `ec1869dae8` with the changes uncommitted in the working tree. `scratch/after.txt` and `scratch/repro-after.txt` are the coordinator's records. \"Close-out rerun\" marks a read-only check rerun from the final tree on 2026-11-13. A code citation names the line the check reads.\n\n| AC-ID | REQ | Given / When / Then | Verification | Status | Waiver |\n|-------|-----|---------------------|--------------|--------|--------|\n| AC-001 | REQ-001 | Given an agent request ending in each of the four no-edit wordings, When the attach path, the scorer gate and the explainer test read it, Then no command attaches, the gate says `false` and a read-only request reads as read-only | `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`, `VX tests/command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts` and `VX tests/scorer/read-only-explainer.vitest.ts` report 0 failed with the T003 to T005 cases, and `probe-no-edit.mts` prints `undefined` on its five attach lines and `false` on its five scorer lines. Observed: `VALL` reads `Tests 1796 passed` with 0 failed at `scratch/after.txt:19`, which includes the three files, and the five attach lines and five scorer lines end at `scratch/repro-after.txt:96` and `scratch/repro-after.txt:101` with `-> undefined` and `-> false` on each | Met | - |\n| AC-002 | REQ-002 | Given the before lines in `scratch/before.txt`, When T038 reruns `FLOOR` and `EVAL` after the rebuild, Then every value equals its before line | `scratch/after.txt` ends `RESULT: every floor equals its before line`. Observed: `scratch/after.txt:63` is that line, and its four `FLOOR` lines and `EVAL` `[160,50,21,5]` equal the lines in `scratch/before.txt` | Met | - |\n| AC-003 | REQ-003 | Given a run log line naming a folder with a fake advisor CLI and hook and no arena marker, When the backfill runs, Then neither fake runs and the line holds `offerError` `untrusted_checkout` | The T010 cases pass in `VX tests/command-offer.vitest.ts`, and `probe-backfill-trust.mjs` prints `fake CLI ran: false, fake hook ran: false`. Observed: `VALL` 0 failed, `scratch/repro-after.txt:25` prints `fake CLI ran: false, fake hook ran: false` and the next line prints `offerError: \"untrusted_checkout\"` | Met | - |\n| AC-004 | REQ-004 | Given a turn that creates `notes draft.md` and `plain.md`, When the restore runs, Then both files are gone and nothing is left over | The T011 cases pass in `VX tests/worktree-restore.vitest.ts`, and `probe-restore-quoted.mjs` prints `left on disk: notes draft.md false, plain.md false`. Observed: `VALL` 0 failed, and `scratch/repro-after.txt:157` prints `left on disk: notes draft.md false, plain.md false` after `\"restored\":true` and `\"leftoverPaths\":[]` | Met | - |\n| AC-005 | REQ-005 | Given a selection of started-command ids with no `--arm`, When the runner picks the arm, Then it is `g2`, and a selection mixing them with other ids is refused with `mixed_row_arms` | The T012 cases pass in `VX tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts`, and `probe-arm-fixture.mjs` prints `-> arm g2` and `arm refused mixed_row_arms`. Observed: `VALL` 0 failed, `scratch/repro-after.txt:14` prints `--row-id g2-deep-review-ask -> arm g2` and `scratch/repro-after.txt:16` prints `-> arm refused mixed_row_arms` | Met | - |\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"3:description: \"Review pass two confirmed 27 P2 findings and no P0 or P1. Four no-edit wordings still attach a writing command, a backfill runs code from any folder a run log names, a file name with a space survives the restore and the doctor checks misread common hook launches. This phase fixes all 27 in ten file-disjoint work groups, with a failing-then-passing test wherever one can fail, and moves no floor.\"\n48:- One no-edit test shared by the attach path, the scorer's two command gates and the read-only explainer, which catches the common straight and curly wordings and moves no floor.\n59:Four no-edit wordings, \"don't change anything yet\", \"no changes yet\", \"don't touch any files\" written with a curly apostrophe and \"make no changes\", still attach `/create:agent` on the hub path and still pass the scorer's command gate, because the shared pattern knows only \"do not\". A backfill runs whatever advisor CLI and prompt hook sit in a folder a run log names. A created file whose name holds a space survives the restore. A started-command row picked with `--row-id` runs under the default arm, and its backfill replays a different fixture than the run used. The command capture leaves six environment variables changed in its caller, the cost script measures the child brief inside a dispatched worker and a busy marker after 1 MiB of stderr gets no retry. The hook-wiring check reports `hook-missing` for `env node`, `bash -lc` and five more working launches, and A10 counts two report-only copies as expected. Nine docs, comments and contracts say something the code no longer does.\n93:# PL/probe-no-edit.mts, exit 0\n113:# PL/probe-no-edit-corpus.mjs, exit 0\n283:- A. Widen the shared no-edit pattern, normalise curly apostrophes before the test in one exported helper and route the attach path, the scorer's two gates and the explainer through it. Guard status privacy with a stored record, drop the vacuous assertion, name `mutating` in the README row shape and escape line breaks in `tsString` (WG1).\n328:| REQ-001 | `SA2-P2-002`: `command-attach.ts` exports `isNoEditRequest(text)`, which lowercases, maps U+2018 and U+2019 to a straight apostrophe and tests a `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` widened with `make no changes`, `no changes yet` and the `don't` contraction. The plan first named a bare `no changes`, which a verifier showed catching change requests that limit their scope, so T042 narrowed it. `attachCommand`, `readOnlyRouteAllowed`, `commandMeaningEligible` and `isReadOnlyExplainer` call it, so the four wordings attach no command, fail both gates and read as no-write on a read-only prompt. |\n373:- **SC-001**: The planning probes print the fixed behaviour: `probe-no-edit.mts` prints `undefined` on all five attach lines and `false` on all five scorer lines, `probe-backfill-trust.mjs` prints `fake CLI ran: false, fake hook ran: false`, `probe-restore-quoted.mjs` prints `left on disk: notes draft.md false, plain.md false`, `probe-arm-fixture.mjs` prints `--row-id g2-deep-review-ask -> arm g2` and `refused mixed_row_arms`, `probe-capture-env.mjs` prints `variables left changed: []`, `probe-cost-child.mjs` prints `hook saw AI_SESSION_CHILD=<unset>`, `probe-busy-cap.mts` prints `marker after 1 MiB: errorCode SQLITE_BUSY_EXHAUSTED, retriesAttempted 1`, `probe-hook-shapes.cjs` prints `exit 0 ok claude` for the nine launch shapes and `hook-missing` for both `echo` shapes, and `probe-a10-count.sh` prints `3/6 copies as expected, 2 reported only, 1 pointer missing`.\n421:- \"do not change anything yet\" still matches, and a prompt with no no-edit wording still attaches `/create:agent`.\n434:| Risk | 9/25 | The no-edit gate and the backfill trust are offer-safety and code-execution guards, each behind a failing-then-passing test and the floors |\n---AC001---\n## 2. CRITERIA\n\nOne row per criterion. `AC-ID` is stable once written: supersede a criterion, never renumber it. A new row takes the highest AC-ID plus one. The short names are the ones `tasks.md` defines in its Task Notation. Every reading ran on base commit `ec1869dae8` with the changes uncommitted in the working tree. `scratch/after.txt` and `scratch/repro-after.txt` are the coordinator's records. \"Close-out rerun\" marks a read-only check rerun from the final tree on 2026-11-13. A code citation names the line the check reads.\n\n| AC-ID | REQ | Given / When / Then | Verification | Status | Waiver |\n|-------|-----|---------------------|--------------|--------|--------|\n| AC-001 | REQ-001 | Given an agent request ending in each of the four no-edit wordings, When the attach path, the scorer gate and the explainer test read it, Then no command attaches, the gate says `false` and a read-only request reads as read-only | `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`, `VX tests/command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts` and `VX tests/scorer/read-only-explainer.vitest.ts` report 0 failed with the T003 to T005 cases, and `probe-no-edit.mts` prints `undefined` on its five attach lines and `false` on its five scorer lines. Observed: `VALL` reads `Tests 1796 passed` with 0 failed at `scratch/after.txt:19`, which includes the three files, and the five attach lines and five scorer lines end at `scratch/repro-after.txt:96` and `scratch/repro-after.txt:101` with `-> undefined` and `-> false` on each | Met | - |\n| AC-002 | REQ-002 | Given the before lines in `scratch/before.txt`, When T038 reruns `FLOOR` and `EVAL` after the rebuild, Then every value equals its before line | `scratch/after.txt` ends `RESULT: every floor equals its before line`. Observed: `scratch/after.txt:63` is that line, and its four `FLOOR` lines and `EVAL` `[160,50,21,5]` equal the lines in `scratch/before.txt` | Met | - |\n| AC-003 | REQ-003 | Given a run log line naming a folder with a fake advisor CLI and hook and no arena marker, When the backfill runs, Then neither fake runs and the line holds `offerError` `untrusted_checkout` | The T010 cases pass in `VX tests/command-offer.vitest.ts`, and `probe-backfill-trust.mjs` prints `fake CLI ran: false, fake hook ran: false`. Observed: `VALL` 0 failed, `scratch/repro-after.txt:25` prints `fake CLI ran: false, fake hook ran: false` and the next line prints `offerError: \"untrusted_checkout\"` | Met | - |\n| AC-004 | REQ-004 | Given a turn that creates `notes draft.md` and `plain.md`, When the restore runs, Then both files are gone and nothing is left over | The T011 cases pass in `VX tests/worktree-restore.vitest.ts`, and `probe-restore-quoted.mjs` prints `left on disk: notes draft.md false, plain.md false`. Observed: `VALL` 0 failed, and `scratch/repro-after.txt:157` prints `left on disk: notes draft.md false, plain.md false` after `\"restored\":true` and `\"leftoverPaths\":[]` | Met | - |\n| AC-005 | REQ-005 | Given a selection of started-command ids with no `--arm`, When the runner picks the arm, Then it is `g2`, and a selection mixing them with other ids is refused with `mixed_row_arms` | The T012 cases pass in `VX tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts`, and `probe-arm-fixture.mjs` prints `-> arm g2` and `arm refused mixed_row_arms`. Observed: `VALL` 0 failed, `scratch/repro-after.txt:14` prints `--row-id g2-deep-review-ask -> arm g2` and `scratch/repro-after.txt:16` prints `-> arm refused mixed_row_arms` | Met | - |\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && rg -n \\\"REQ-001|no-edit wording|no-edit\\\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/spec.md | head -20 && echo \\\"---AC001---\\\" && sed -n '50,60p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remedia