{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794595963208,"sessionID":"ses_e29cd1063ffeCxGmp1qmJeHmTZ","part":{"partID":"prt_1d6413e72001djeWvan8uYUq1f","sessionID":"ses_e29cd1063ffeCxGmp1qmJeHmTZ","messageID":"msg_1d641162000181V6tDErwg8KT3","type":"tool","id":"call_0d7edaa016a7420ea3e85afa","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && rg -n \"no-edit|NO_EDIT|make no changes\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/ .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/ 2>/dev/null | head -12"},"output":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md:36:A meaning pass lifts a command past the read-only confidence floor, so `commandMeaningEligible` asks the question that floor asks of a phrase match. A prompt matching `NO_EDIT_REQUEST`, such as \"no edits\", \"do not change\", \"just show\" or \"just list\", rules out every command on meaning. A read-only explainer prompt admits only a command marked `readOnly`, because running it is the answer. `readOnlyRouteAllowed` reads the same pattern, so the two gates cannot drift apart.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md:33:When a recommendation gets a `compiledRoute`, `enrichCompiledRoutes()` also asks `attachCommand()` in `lib/command-attach.ts` for a slash command and sets the optional `command` field when one comes back (the `command` field of `AdvisorRecommendationSchema` in `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts`, `z.string().min(1).optional()`). `attachCommand()` names a command only for a `route` decision with `selectionKind: 'single'` and exactly one target, and only when the generated `MODE_COMMANDS` table maps that hub and `workflowMode` to a command. A bundle, a multi-target route or a mode with no command leaves `command` off. For `system-deep-loop` the prompt must type the same command or hold a phrase from `DEPTH_WORDING`, so a prompt that only names a topic such as research or review gets no deep-loop command. A prompt that matches `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` gets no command from any hub, because a reader who rules out a change is never handed work that writes.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md:36:A meaning pass lifts a command past the read-only confidence floor, so `commandMeaningEligible` asks the question that floor asks of a phrase match. A prompt matching `NO_EDIT_REQUEST`, such as \"no edits\", \"do not change\", \"just show\" or \"just list\", rules out every command on meaning. A read-only explainer prompt admits only a command marked `readOnly`, because running it is the answer. `readOnlyRouteAllowed` reads the same pattern, so the two gates cannot drift apart.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md:33:When a recommendation gets a `compiledRoute`, `enrichCompiledRoutes()` also asks `attachCommand()` in `lib/command-attach.ts` for a slash command and sets the optional `command` field when one comes back (the `command` field of `AdvisorRecommendationSchema` in `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts`, `z.string().min(1).optional()`). `attachCommand()` names a command only for a `route` decision with `selectionKind: 'single'` and exactly one target, and only when the generated `MODE_COMMANDS` table maps that hub and `workflowMode` to a command. A bundle, a multi-target route or a mode with no command leaves `command` off. For `system-deep-loop` the prompt must type the same command or hold a phrase from `DEPTH_WORDING`, so a prompt that only names a topic such as research or review gets no deep-loop command. A prompt that matches `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` gets no command from any hub, because a reader who rules out a change is never handed work that writes.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && rg -n \\\"no-edit|NO_EDIT|make no changes\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/ .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/ 2>/dev/null | head -12\"}"},"time":{"start":1794595962482,"end":1794595963208}}}}
