{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794596014268,"sessionID":"ses_e29cd1063ffeCxGmp1qmJeHmTZ","part":{"partID":"prt_1d641f311002FBcI67ogs0Y7el","sessionID":"ses_e29cd1063ffeCxGmp1qmJeHmTZ","messageID":"msg_1d641cbcb001Zy3Knp1J1bxUtL","type":"tool","id":"call_112da8d8fa2d43478beae7d1","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"- Running the same prompt through the pre-commit module extracted with `git show 860610d783^:...` and the current module: the before/after delta for a predicate change is measured, not asserted (iteration 2).\n- Tracing each changed surface to its owning phase packet (`017-review-pass-two-remediation` REQ-001, AC-001, AC-027) and to the feature-catalog promise, which separated \"criterion met as written\" from \"product promise violated\" (iteration 3).","oldString":"- Running the same prompt through the pre-commit module extracted with `git show 860610d783^:...` and the current module: the before/after delta for a predicate change is measured, not asserted (iteration 2).","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/hook-confirm-3b/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/hook-confirm-3b/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/hook-confirm-3b/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/hook-confirm-3b/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/hook-confirm-3b/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/hook-confirm-3b/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -57,8 +57,9 @@\n ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n - Driving the real CLI against a settings root per command: `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs --root <probe>` distinguishes the fix from a regression in one run, and the paired `printf '' | node - <script>` probe proves what node actually executes rather than what the reader assumes (iteration 1).\n - Reading the flag grammar from node's own behaviour (`node -rc /dev/null` -> `bad option`) instead of inferring it from the flag tables (iteration 1).\n - Running the same prompt through the pre-commit module extracted with `git show 860610d783^:...` and the current module: the before/after delta for a predicate change is measured, not asserted (iteration 2).\n+- Tracing each changed surface to its owning phase packet (`017-review-pass-two-remediation` REQ-001, AC-001, AC-027) and to the feature-catalog promise, which separated \"criterion met as written\" from \"product promise violated\" (iteration 3).\n \n ## 8A. WHAT FAILED\n - Relying on the commit's suite claim as evidence: the dispatch permits only the two named single test files, so the claim was treated as unverified prose and the CLI probes carried the proof instead (iteration 1).\n - Trusting a green guard suite as evidence that a predicate change is safe: the suite passed 26/26 while a genuine no-edit prompt was misrouted, because no row exercises `make no changes to <object>` as a no-edit request (iteration 2).\n","status":"modified","additions":1,"deletions":0}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/hook-confirm-3b/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\":\"- Running the same prompt through the pre-commit module extracted with `git show 860610d783^:...` and the current module: the before/after delta for a predicate change is measured, not asserted (iteration 2).\\n- Tracing each changed surface to its owning phase packet (`017-review-pass-two-remediation` REQ-001, AC-001, AC-027) and to the feature-catalog promise, which separated \\\"criterion met as written\\\" from \\\"product promise violated\\\" (iteration 3).\",\"oldString\":\"- Running the same prompt through the pre-commit module extracted with `git show 860610d783^:...` and the current module: the before/after delta for a predicate change is measured, not asserted (iteration 2).\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/hook-confirm-3b/deep-review-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794596008721,"end":1794596014268}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794596014273,"sessionID":"ses_e29cd1063ffeCxGmp1qmJeHmTZ","part":{"partID":"prt_1d641f9e70019n0amss1EV37d0","sessionID":"ses_e29cd1063ffeCxGmp1qmJeHmTZ","messageID":"msg_1d641cbcb001Zy3Knp1J1bxUtL","type":"tool","id":"call_7e6eb07162454ff981e74ab7","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"- Trusting a green guard suite as evidence that a predicate change is safe: the suite passed 26/26 while a genuine no-edit prompt was misrouted, because no row exercises `make no changes to <object>` as a no-edit request (iteration 2).\n- Reading AC-001's `Met` row as blanket coverage of the no-edit gate: it is scoped to requests *ending* in a no-edit phrase and never claims the object-bearing class (iteration 3).","oldString":"- Trusting a green guard suite as evidence that a predicate change is safe: the suite passed 26/26 while a genuine no-edit prompt was misrouted, because no row exercises `make no changes to <object>` as a no-edit request (iteration 2).","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/hook-confirm-3b/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/hook-confirm-3b/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/hook-confirm-3b/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/hook-confirm-3b/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/hook-confirm-3b/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/hook-confirm-3b/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -62,8 +62,9 @@\n \n ## 8A. WHAT FAILED\n - Relying on the commit's suite claim as evidence: the dispatch permits only the two named single test files, so the claim was treated as unverified prose and the CLI probes carried the proof instead (iteration 1).\n - Trusting a green guard suite as evidence that a predicate change is safe: the suite passed 26/26 while a genuine no-edit prompt was misrouted, because no row exercises `make no changes to <object>` as a no-edit request (iteration 2).\n+- Reading AC-001's `Met` row as blanket coverage of the no-edit gate: it is scoped to requests *ending* in a no-edit phrase and never claims the object-bearing class (iteration 3).\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n ## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n ### \"A caller compensates with a second check\": ruled out by reading all three call sites — none inspects the sentence beyond the predicate. -- BLOCKED (iteration 2, 1 attempts)\n","status":"modified","additions":1,"deletions":0}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/hook-confirm-3b/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\":\"- Trusting a green guard suite as evidence that a predicate change is safe: the suite passed 26/26 while a genuine no-edit prompt was misrouted, because no row exercises `make no changes to <object>` as a no-edit request (iteration 2).\\n- Reading AC-001's `Met` row as blanket coverage of the no-edit gate: it is scoped to requests *ending* in a no-edit phrase and never claims the object-bearing class (iteration 3).\",\"oldString\":\"- Trusting a green guard suite as evidence that a predicate change is safe: the suite passed 26/26 while a genuine no-edit prompt was misrouted, because no row exercises `make no changes to <object>` as a no-edit request (iteration 2).\",\"path\":\"spec